UPDATE companies SET description='Consolidated Telcom, headquartered in Dickinson, North Dakota, traces its roots to January 2, 1961, when the Bowman‑Slope Rural Telephone Mutual Aid Corporation and the Dunn Telephone Mutual Aid Corporation merged to form the Consolidated Telephone Cooperative. The cooperative is owned by its members—customers who use its services—and governed by an elected board of directors.

The company provides telecommunications services across southwestern North Dakota, including fiber‑to‑the‑home internet, cable television, voice, and business services such as cybersecurity and camera solutions. Since 2005 it has built a 100% fiber‑to‑the‑home network in its cooperative exchanges, serving 19 communities, and is extending fiber upgrades to its competitive local exchange carrier (CLEC) territory in Dickinson, Belfield, and Gladstone. Operations also include a CATV system acquired in 2000 that now covers the entire cooperative service area.

Consolidated serves residential and business customers in rural and small‑town markets across southwestern North Dakota. Its customer base includes households, farms, ranches, and enterprises such as Dickinson State University, which became its first CLEC client in 1998. The cooperative model aims to deliver urban‑level services at affordable rates to communities that larger carriers often overlook.

Founded to bring essential telephone service to areas where commercial providers found it unprofitable, the cooperative remains driven by its mission to “empower our communities by delivering advanced telecommunications products and services and building reliable, future‑ready infrastructure.” Its structure returns revenues above operating costs to members as capital credits, aligning incentives with customer needs rather than shareholder profit.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fiber\u2011to\u2011the\u2011home network deployment", "Cable TV (CATV) distribution", "Voice telephone service", "Business internet and managed services", "Cybersecurity services", "Security camera installation and monitoring", "Competitive local exchange carrier (CLEC) operations"], "industries": ["Residential", "Business", "Education"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% fiber\u2011to\u2011the\u2011home in all cooperative exchanges", "Cooperative ownership returning capital credits to members", "CLEC operations extending competitive services to Dickinson, Belfield, Gladstone", "CATV system covering entire cooperative service area", "Mission to provide urban\u2011comparable services at affordable rates"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1961 as Consolidated Telephone Cooperative from merger of Bowman\u2011Slope and Dunn Mutual Aid Corporations -> /about", "Headquarters in Dickinson, North Dakota -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label) and /about", "Member\u2011owned cooperative structure with elected board -> /about", "100% fiber\u2011to\u2011the\u2011home in cooperative exchanges serving 19 communities -> /about", "CLEC operations since 1998; Dickinson State University first CLEC customer -> /about", "CATV system acquired 2000 covering cooperative service area -> /about", "Services: Internet, TV, Phone, Business Services, Camera Solutions, cyberSECURITY -> / and /about", "Mission statement and capital credits description -> /about", "Board of directors listed -> /about", "Description as premier telecommunication provider since 1961 -> db (description)"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Consolidated is the premier provider of telecommunication services in Southwestern North Dakota since 1961.", "founded_year": "1961", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='consolidated-telcom' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Container and Packaging operates from Boise, Idaho, as a wholesale distributor of bottles, jars, closures, and packaging supplies. The company sources its inventory from a worldwide network of manufacturing partners, offering containers in plastic (including PET, HDPE, and PP), glass, metal, and post-consumer recycled (PCR) resins.

Beyond stock packaging, the company provides in-house decoration services such as screen printing, hot foil stamping, and shrink sleeves, along with custom box manufacturing, packaging design consultation, label printing, warehousing, logistics, and dedicated sourcing for custom or complex projects.

Its customer base spans food and beverage, personal care, pharmaceuticals, essential oils, nutrition and supplements, pet care, art supplies, and chemical and industrial markets. The company highlights work with small brands and startups—including Lone Star Bee Co., Amallow Skincare, and Brwnsgr Skincare—that order volumes from a handful of units up to several thousand.

Container and Packaging differentiates itself through personalized account management: representatives offer quick quote turnaround (often same-day), multiple shipping options, pre-purchase samples, and hands-on problem solving. The company encourages customers to call for custom needs, framing its team as a sourcing partner that can locate items not found in the online catalog.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Screen printing", "Hot foil stamping", "Shrink sleeves", "Custom boxes", "Packaging design", "Labels & printing", "Warehousing & logistics", "Sourcing"], "industries": ["Food Storage", "Chemical & Industrial", "Pharmaceutical", "Essential Oils", "Art Supply", "Pet Care", "Nutrition & Supplement", "Food & Beverage", "Personal Care"], "materials": ["PET", "HDPE", "PP", "Glass", "Metal", "Post-Consumer-Resin (PCR)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Human-assisted sourcing for custom and hard-to-find packaging", "In-house decoration: screen printing, hot foil stamping, shrink sleeves", "Integrated warehousing, logistics, and packaging design services", "Personalized account representatives with same-day quote response", "Samples provided before large orders"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Boise, Idaho -> db", "Product categories: plastic, glass, recycled, metal, closures -> /", "Materials: PET, HDPE, PP, PCR, glass, metal -> /", "Decoration services: screen printing, hot foil stamping, shrink sleeves -> / (capabilities, services)", "Additional services: custom boxes, packaging design, labels & printing, warehousing & logistics, sourcing -> / (services)", "Industries served: Food Storage, Chemical & Industrial, Pharmaceutical, Essential Oils, Art Supply, Pet Care, Nutrition & Supplement, Food & Beverage, Personal Care -> / (Shop By Industry)", "Customer examples: Lone Star Bee Co., Amallow Skincare, Brwnsgr Skincare -> / (customer stories)", "Differentiators: personalized account reps, quick quotes, multiple shipping options, samples, human-assisted sourcing -> / (testimonials, homepage text)", "Company type: wholesale distributor -> / (page title)", "Worldwide network of manufacturing partners -> / (products list)"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Wholesale Bottles, Jars & Packaging Supplies", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='container-and-packaging' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Contempora Fabrics, founded in 1972 by Lacy C. Nance, is an employee-owned circular knit manufacturer based in Lumberton, North Carolina. The company began as a contract knitter producing fine gauge interlock and single knit fabrics, and transitioned to full employee ownership through an ESOP in 1988.

Today the company operates 175 circular knitting machines in a 150,000-square-foot facility on 29 acres, with a monthly capacity of 2 million pounds of fabric. It offers both greige and finished fabrics, supported by an in-house research and development team that provides fabric analysis and works with the latest fiber technologies. The lint-controlled, humidity-defined manufacturing environment allows simultaneous processing of all fiber types.

Contempora serves brands, retailers, and manufacturers across performance and activewear, athletic and team apparel, fashion and formal wear, casual and career wear, intimate apparel and shapewear, and swimwear and beachwear. Its client base includes companies such as Boombah, and the staff has extensive experience handling USMCA and CAFTA-DR shipping requirements for weekly container shipments to Central America.

The company emphasizes its ESOP culture as a driver of quality and on-time delivery, alongside sustainability initiatives that have reduced energy consumption through lighting upgrades and recycling of byproducts such as cardboard tubes, scrap yarn, and plastic. Competitive pricing and short lead times are cited as daily commitments.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Circular knitting (coarse and fine gauge)", "Greige goods production", "Finished fabric production", "Fabric analysis", "Research & development", "Greige goods sales", "Finished fabric sales", "Sustainability initiatives (energy efficiency, recycling)", "International shipping compliance (USMCA/CAFTA-DR)"], "industries": ["Performance & Activewear", "Athletic & Team Apparel", "Fashion & Formal Wear", "Casual & Career Wear", "Intimate Apparel & Shapewear", "Swimwear & Beachwear"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Capacity of 2 million pounds per month", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% employee-owned (ESOP) structure", "Lint-controlled, humidity-defined manufacturing process", "In-house R&D and fabric analysis capabilities", "Expertise in USMCA and CAFTA-DR international shipping compliance", "Sustainability program including energy-efficient upgrades and byproduct recycling"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 by Lacy C. Nance -> /about-us", "Employee-owned (ESOP) since 1988 -> /about-us", "Located in Lumberton, NC -> /", "175 machines, 150,000 sq ft facility, 29 acres -> /about-us", "Capacity 2 million pounds per month -> /about-us", "Industries served list -> /", "Client Boombah testimonial -> /", "USMCA/CAFTA-DR shipping experience -> /", "Sustainability practices -> /", "R&D and fabric analysis -> /services", "Greige and finished fabric sales -> /services", "Lint-controlled, humidity-defined process -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today Contempora Fabrics operates 175 machines in a 150,000 square foot facility on 29 acres and is known for a versatile product mix and capacity to manufacture 2 million pounds of fabric each month.", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["USMCA", "CAFTA-DR"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='contempora-fabrics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cope Plastics Inc operates a fabrication and distribution branch in Fargo, North Dakota, supported by its headquarters in Alton, Illinois. The Fargo facility sits about four miles from Hector International Airport and serves as a regional hub for custom plastic fabrication and material supply.

The branch runs advanced CNC equipment — saws, routers, and drills — to produce custom plastic parts, prototypes, and cut-to-size components. Its 7,000-square-foot warehouse stocks a range of engineering plastics including sheets, rods, and tubes in materials such as ACM, acrylic, HDPE, nylon, polycarbonate, polyurethane, and UHMW. The company also fabricates specialized components like pistons, thrust washers, rollers, bushings, and boom pads for industrial equipment.

Cope Plastics serves industries including fluid handling, food and beverage, construction, mining operations, material handling, and safety and security. Customers range from food-processing plants needing lubricant-free rollers to mining operations using nylon sheaves for forklifts and crane boom pads. The company also supplies conduit duct spacers, ground protection mats, and outrigger pads for construction and utility applications.

The company emphasizes a streamlined manufacturing process and rigorous quality control to minimize lead times, distinguishing itself from standard plastic distributors by offering USA-made fabricated parts alongside stocked materials. Local delivery is available on qualifying orders.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC sawing", "CNC routing", "CNC drilling", "Custom plastic fabrication", "Prototyping", "Cut-to-size machining", "Plastic sheet, rod, and tube distribution", "Local pickup", "Local delivery (qualifying orders)"], "industries": ["Fluid Handling", "Food & Beverage", "Construction", "Mining Operations", "Material Handling", "Safety & Security"], "materials": ["ACM", "Acrylic", "Foam PVC", "Fluted Polypropylene", "Flexible Tubing", "HDPE", "HDPE Cutting Board", "Nylon", "Polycarbonate", "Polyurethane", "UHMW", "Conduit duct spacers", "Ground protection mats", "Outrigger pads", "Urethane Patches"], "equipment": ["CNC saws", "CNC routers", "CNC drills"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Headquarters in Alton, IL houses the largest collection of CNC plastic fabrication equipment in the Midwest", "Streamlined manufacturing process for efficient production and exceptional quality", "USA-made custom plastic parts fabricated in-house", "Rigorous quality control on all stocked and fabricated materials", "Local delivery on qualifying orders in the Fargo region"], "facts_used": ["Fargo branch location 4 miles from Hector International Airport -> /", "Headquarters in Alton, IL with largest CNC plastic fabrication equipment collection in Midwest -> /", "7,000 sq ft warehouse in Fargo -> /", "CNC equipment: saws, routers, drills -> /", "Custom plastic parts, prototypes, cut-to-size -> /", "Stocked materials: ACM, Acrylic, Foam PVC, Fluted Polypropylene, Flexible Tubing, HDPE, HDPE Cutting Board, Nylon, Polycarbonate, Polyurethane, UHMW, Conduit duct spacers, Ground protection mats, Outrigger pads, Urethane Patches -> /", "Industries served: Fluid Handling, Food & Beverage, Construction, Mining Operations, Material Handling, Safety & Security -> /", "Example parts: pistons, thrust washers, rollers, bushings, boom pads, nylon sheaves -> /", "Streamlined manufacturing process, rigorous quality control, USA-made parts -> /", "Local delivery on qualifying orders -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our team of fabrication experts operates advanced CNC equipment, including saws, routers, and drills, to meet all your custom fabrication needs.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cope-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Copper Star Home Medical Supplies operates from Phoenix, Arizona, where it has served the metropolitan area for over 22 years. The company runs what it describes as the largest medical supply showroom in the state, with additional locations in Tempe, Mesa, and Surprise.

The retailer stocks a broad range of durable medical equipment for sale or weekly and monthly rental. Inventory includes power lift chairs, hospital beds, manual and power wheelchairs, mobility scooters, walkers, rollators, CPAP and BiPAP machines, portable and stationary oxygen concentrators, knee scooters, patient lifts, bath safety equipment, compression garments, orthopedic bracing, and daily living aids. All showroom units are fully assembled for hands‑on evaluation before purchase or rental.

Customers include patients recovering from surgery, individuals managing chronic conditions, seasonal “snowbird” residents, and caregivers. The company works directly with Medicare, Aetna, Blue Cross Blue Shield of Arizona, Devoted Health, Homelink, Integrated Home Care Services, One Call, and Prospect Medical Group, and accepts FSA and HSA payments. Healthcare professionals also refer patients for equipment fitting and procurement.

Copper Star emphasizes a consultative approach: staff help clients decide between renting and buying, navigate insurance coverage, and select equipment suited to Arizona’s climate and the needs of an aging population. Its Bell Road location sits near HonorHealth Deer Valley Medical Center and Mayo Clinic Hospital, supporting post‑discharge transitions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Retail sales of durable medical equipment", "Equipment rental (weekly and monthly)", "Insurance verification and billing", "FSA/HSA payment processing", "Product demonstration and fitting", "Patient equipment consultation"], "industries": ["Home medical equipment", "Durable medical equipment (DME)", "Post\u2011discharge recovery", "In\u2011home care", "Respiratory therapy", "Mobility assistance", "Orthopedic bracing", "Sleep therapy", "Oxygen therapy"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest medical supply showroom in Arizona", "Fully assembled equipment available for in\u2011store trial", "Sale, short\u2011term, and long\u2011term rental options", "In\u2011house insurance verification and billing for Medicare and major private plans", "Four Phoenix\u2011metro locations near major hospitals"], "facts_used": ["Phoenix, AZ headquarters -> db", "Over 22 years in business -> /", "Largest medical supply showroom in Arizona -> /", "Additional locations in Tempe, Mesa, Surprise -> /", "Product categories: power lift chairs, hospital beds, wheelchairs, scooters, walkers, rollators, CPAP/BiPAP, oxygen concentrators, knee scooters, patient lifts, bath safety, compression garments, orthopedic bracing, daily living aids -> /", "Sale and weekly/monthly rental options -> /", "Fully assembled showroom units for trial -> /", "Insurance partners: Medicare, Aetna, BCBS AZ, Devoted Health, Homelink, Integrated Home Care Services, One Call, Prospect Medical Group -> /", "Accepts FSA/HSA payments -> /", "Serves patients, caregivers, snowbirds, healthcare professionals -> /", "Consultative approach: rent vs buy guidance, insurance navigation -> /", "Location near HonorHealth Deer Valley Medical Center and Mayo Clinic Hospital -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Copper Star Home Medical has been Phoenix''s locally trusted home medical equipment store for over 22 years.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='copper-star-home-medical-supplies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Copper Wolf Custom Fabrication operates from Golden, Colorado, in the foothills of the Rocky Mountains. The business traces its inception to 2014, when Chris “CL” Long and Rebecca Long met in welding school and later turned their shared trade into a company. The couple, who had previously run a fabrication shop together, formally launched their own venture in 2018.

The shop produces custom metalwork for both residential and commercial clients. Its portfolio includes handmade furnishings, decorative pieces, garden gates, handrails, stair systems, and structural railings. Every item is fabricated to order using 100 % American‑grade steel and reclaimed lumber, then finished with an indoor/outdoor‑rated powder coat.

Customers range from homeowners seeking one‑of‑a‑kind interior and exterior accents to businesses needing custom architectural metalwork. The company cites projects for private homes and commercial spaces alike, and it holds a membership in the Golden Chamber of Commerce.

The founders emphasize material provenance and finish durability as their differentiators: domestic steel, recycled wood, and a powder‑coat system rated for harsh outdoor exposure. They position the shop as a source for bespoke, American‑made metal pieces rather than volume production.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal fabrication", "Welding", "Powder coating", "Metal railings", "Metal stairs", "Custom furnishings", "Decorative metalwork", "Garden gates", "Handrails"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Architectural metalwork", "Interior design"], "materials": ["American-grade steel", "Recycled lumber", "Powder coat"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% American-grade steel and recycled lumber in every piece", "Indoor/outdoor-rated powder coat finish", "Fully custom, made-to-order fabrication", "Husband-and-wife ownership with welding-school roots"], "facts_used": ["Location: Golden, Colorado -> db", "Founding year: 2014 (inception) -> /", "Founders: Chris (CL) Long and Rebecca Long -> /", "Ownership: Family-owned, small business -> /", "Products: custom handmade furnishings, decor, garden gates, handrails, railings, stairs -> /", "Materials: 100% American grade steel, recycled lumber, powder coat -> /", "Processes: welding, fabrication, powder coating -> /", "Industries: residential (home), commercial (business) -> /", "Chamber membership: Golden Chamber of Commerce -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "CWCF specializes in all custom handmade furnishings, decor, garden gates, handrails, as well as many other custom pieces. All items are custom-made to order.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='copper-wolf-custom-fabrication' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Corbitt Manufacturing Company operates from a 100,000-square-foot facility in Paragould, Arkansas. Founded in 1948, the business began as a diversified contract manufacturer specializing in permanent-mold aluminum castings, machined components, custom tooling, and complete assemblies. In 2019, the company was acquired by The Greenbrier Companies and now operates as a Greenbrier subsidiary.

The plant houses three CNC machining centers and three furnaces feeding multiple pour lines, supported by grinders, broaching machines, milling machines, lathes, and a range of presses including a Dake 375-ton hydraulic press, a Bliss SC2 500-ton press, and a Niagara HBM 175-ton press. Standard permanent-mold castings run up to 75 pounds with a maximum mold envelope of 48 by 62 inches, while machining services cover prototype design, reverse engineering, wire and RAM EDM, gear cutting, jig and fixture building, and assembly. Production volumes span from one-off prototypes to several hundred thousand units annually.

Corbitt serves OEMs in earth-moving, mining, agricultural, electrical, transportation, recreation, and food-service markets. In transportation it produces dock cleats, transmission casings, manifolds, and railroad-car parts as the industry shifts from iron to aluminum. For food service it re-engineered a motor housing that eliminated leakage and cut scrap rates. Electrical work includes explosion-proof receptacles and power-line connectors, while powertrain projects focus on light- and heavy-duty gearboxes held to super-close tolerances.

The company emphasizes a "what you need, when and where you need it" delivery guarantee backed by in-house testing protocols that fast-track part deployment. Engineering staff provide troubleshooting expertise on every project, positioning Corbitt as a problem-solving partner rather than a pure production shop.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Permanent-mold aluminum casting", "CNC machining", "Wire EDM", "RAM EDM", "Progressive stamping", "Punching", "Bending", "Welding", "Fabrication", "Hot forming", "Cold forming", "Reverse engineering", "Prototype design", "Tool and die manufacture", "Jig and fixture manufacturing", "Gear manufacturing", "Assembly", "Heat treating", "Finish machining", "Just-in-time delivery"], "industries": ["Earth moving", "Mining", "Agricultural", "Electrical", "Transportation", "Recreation", "Food service", "Powertrain/Transmission"], "materials": ["Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Dake 375-ton hydraulic press", "Bliss SC2 500-ton press", "Niagara HBM 175-ton press", "Neff CNC custom punch unit", "Esab Shadow 2 burn table", "3 CNC machining centers", "3 furnaces", "Grinders", "Broaching machines", "Milling machines", "Lathes", "Blasters", "Casters"], "volume": "Prototypes to several hundred thousand units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Permanent-mold aluminum casting expertise with molds up to 48\u00d762 inches", "In-house testing protocols for fast-tracked deployment", "Production range from prototypes to several hundred thousand units", "Engineering and troubleshooting support on every project", "\"What you need, when and where you need it\" delivery guarantee"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1948 -> /about, /", "Paragould, Arkansas headquarters -> /, /about", "Purchased by The Greenbrier Companies in 2019 -> /about", "100,000 sq. ft. facility -> /about", "3 CNC machining centers and 3 furnaces -> /about", "Production from prototypes to several hundred thousand units -> /about, /services", "Permanent-mold aluminum castings up to 75 lbs, max mold 48x62 inches -> /services", "Equipment: Dake 375-ton hydraulic press, Bliss SC2 500-ton press, Niagara HBM 175-ton press, Neff CNC custom punch unit, Esab Shadow 2 burn table -> /services", "Industries: earth moving, mining, agricultural, electrical, transportation, recreation, food service -> /, /about", "Transportation examples: dock cleats, transmission casings, manifolds, railroad car parts -> /", "Food service example: garbage disposal motor housing redesign -> /", "Electrical examples: explosion-proof receptacles, power line connectors -> /", "Powertrain: light and heavy-duty gearboxes with super-close tolerances -> /", "In-house testing protocols for fast-tracked deployment -> /", "Engineering expertise and troubleshooting -> /", "Delivery guarantee: ''What you need, when and where you need it'' -> /", "Machining services: prototype design, reverse engineering, wire/RAM EDM, gear manufacturing, jig/fixture, assembly -> /services", "Support services: fabrication, hot/cold forming, progressive stamping, punching, bending, welding -> /services", "SolidWorks software -> /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1948, Corbitt Manufacturing Company has specialized in diversified contract-manufacturing.", "founded_year": "1948", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='corbitt-manufacturing-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Corporate Casuals operates from Concord, Massachusetts, where it has been decorating apparel since 1980. The company began as an embroidery studio and, after four years, replaced its original equipment with the production facility it runs today.

The shop specializes in custom embroidery and printing on a wide range of garments and accessories—polo shirts, jackets, fleece, hats, bags, and scrubs—using state-of-the-art embroidery machines and digital printing technology. With a staff of about 15, the facility has decorated well over eight million items to date and is set up for on-demand, single-unit production with no minimum order requirements.

Corporate Casuals sources blank apparel from national warehouses and decorates premium brands such as The North Face, Carhartt, Nike, Under Armour, Marmot, and New Era.

The company emphasizes personal service from industry professionals, free setup on studio designs, and what it describes as the fastest standard processing time in the industry. Its model was built to make single-unit orders profitable, allowing clients to order exactly what they need without inventory risk.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom embroidery", "Custom printing (direct-to-garment/screen)", "Online design center", "Logo upload and digitizing", "On-demand single-unit production", "Free setup on studio designs", "Apparel sourcing from national warehouses"], "industries": ["Corporate/Business", "Small Business", "Organizations/Non-profits", "Promotional Products", "Healthcare (scrubs & lab coats)", "Team Sports/Activewear"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No minimum order quantities", "On-demand single-unit production", "Free setup on all studio designs", "Fastest standard processing time in the industry (as claimed)", "Personal service by industry professionals"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Concord, Massachusetts -> db", "Employee count: 15 -> db", "Founded year: 1980 (Since 1980) -> page:/", "Production facility in Concord, MA -> page:/", "Over 8 million items decorated -> page:/", "Custom embroidery and printing services -> page:/", "No minimum order quantities -> page:/", "On-demand single-unit production -> page:/", "Free setup on studio designs -> page:/", "Fastest standard processing time claimed -> page:/", "Personal service by industry professionals -> page:/", "Brands decorated: The North Face, Carhartt, Nike, Under Armour, Marmot, New Era -> page:/", "Product categories: polo shirts, jackets, fleece, hats, bags, scrubs, activewear -> page:/", "Serves small businesses, organizations, corporate teams -> page:/", "Apparel sourced from national warehouses -> page:/"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_e