UPDATE companies SET description='Cosco Air Conditioning & Refrigeration has served Hawaii’s HVAC contractors from its base in Kailua-Kona since 1961. The family‑owned company was founded to supply the materials and equipment that local air‑conditioning and refrigeration professionals needed, and it has remained under family operation for over six decades.

The business operates a specialty division, Cosco Custom Coils, which manufactures direct‑fit HVAC coils and OEM replacements. The division converts microchannel designs to tube‑and‑fin configurations and produces condenser, evaporator, and chilled‑water coils using copper tube and fin options. In addition to coil fabrication, the company provides machining and metalworking services and applies specialty paints, coatings, and additives. Cosco also acts as the state’s largest Daikin dealer, distributing mini‑split systems and other equipment. The operation employs roughly 50 people.

Primary customers are HVAC contractors across Hawaii, along with commercial and industrial facilities that require heat‑ and energy‑recovery ventilators. The company’s product range covers replacement parts and accessories for air conditioners, refrigeration hardware, and ventilation equipment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Machining & Metalworking", "Specialty Paints, Coatings and Additives", "Custom HVAC coil manufacturing", "Coil conversion (microchannel to tube and fin)", "OEM coil replacement", "Condenser coil fabrication", "Evaporator coil fabrication", "Chilled water coil fabrication", "Copper tube and fin coil options", "Daikin equipment distribution"], "industries": ["Heat & Energy Recovery Ventilators", "HVAC", "Refrigeration", "Air Conditioning"], "materials": ["Copper tube", "Fin stock"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family owned and operated since 1961", "Hawaii\u2019s #1 Daikin dealer", "Custom HVAC coil manufacturing and OEM replacements", "Microchannel to tube\u2011and\u2011fin conversion", "Copper tube and fin coil options"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1961 -> db, /", "Family-owned -> /", "Headquarters Kailua-Kona, Hawaii -> db", "Employee count 50 -> db", "Custom coil manufacturing division -> /", "Daikin dealer -> /", "Machining & Metalworking capability -> db", "Specialty Paints, Coatings and Additives capability -> db", "Industries served: Heat & Energy Recovery Ventilators -> db", "Copper tube and fin materials -> /", "Microchannel conversion -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Cosco Custom Coils Our specialty division provides direct fit custom HVAC coils and OEM replacements", "founded_year": "1961", "employee_count": "50", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cosco-air-conditioning-refrigeration' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cosmos Food Co., Inc. was founded in 1971 in City of Industry, California. The company traces its roots to family recipes brought from Korea, establishing a business centered on authentic kimchi production. No founders are named in the source material.

The company manufactures a range of kimchi varieties — hot, mild, and MSG‑free — using lacto‑fermentation. It positions itself as a one‑stop shop for authentic Korean kimchi in North America, emphasizing manufacturing to high quality and safety standards. Facility size, headcount, and production volumes are not disclosed.

The company does not name specific clients or industries beyond the broader North American market for Korean food products.

