UPDATE companies SET description='Crossfire Technologies Inc, headquartered in St. Paul, Minnesota, develops advanced chiplet interconnect solutions for the semiconductor industry. The company focuses on eliminating the need for traditional silicon interposers through its Bridgelet product line.

Crossfire’s core offerings include Bridgelets — passive or active interconnect devices that replace interposers for chiplet-to-chiplet communication — and Direct Chiplet Input/Output (DCIO), a streamlined PHY interface compatible with standard link layers such as UCIe and Bunch of Wires. The company also provides OmniDie, a proprietary integration capability that physically combines multiple chiplets into a single “SuperChip” mounted directly on a package substrate, reducing reliance on advanced packaging. These technologies support ultra-short-reach signaling (<500 µm), die-scale interconnect densities (sub-micron), and protocol-agnostic operation.

Its solutions are designed to enable chiplet reuse across product families and to disaggregate system I/O from memory functions.

Crossfire positions its technology as an interposer alternative that delivers up to 50× smaller form factor, 10× lower energy per bit, and 10× lower upfront cost, with up to 50 percent reduction in chiplet die area. The company states that its DCIO approach can achieve 10× lower power, cost, and higher density compared to competing solutions, while its OmniDie integration minimizes the need for costly advanced packaging.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Bridgelet design and development (passive/active)", "Direct Chiplet Input/Output (DCIO) implementation", "OmniDie multi-chiplet integration", "Die-to-die PHY integration (UCIe, Bunch of Wires, Ultra Short Reach SerDes)", "Protocol-agnostic link-layer development", "Chiplet reuse architecture consulting", "Advanced packaging alternative solutions"], "industries": ["AI infrastructure", "Semiconductor", "Chiplet ecosystem", "Data center", "High-performance computing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["50\u00d7 smaller, 10\u00d7 less energy per bit, 10\u00d7 lower upfront cost than interposer-based solutions", "Up to 50% reduction in chiplet die area", "Wire-abundant interfaces (1K connections per 0.25 mm\u00b2)", "Ultra-short-reach signaling (<500 \u00b5m) with die-scale interconnect density", "Protocol-agnostic PHY supporting UCIe, BoW, and proprietary D2D solutions"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: St Paul, Minnesota -> db", "Bridgelet products provide chiplet-to-chiplet interconnect alternative to interposers -> /", "Bridgelets can be passive or active -> /", "Compatible with UCIe, BoW, Ultra Short Reach SerDes -> /", "DCIO compatible with standard link layers, provides 10x lower power/cost/density -> /", "OmniDie enables SuperChip integration minimizing advanced packaging -> /", "Targets AI infrastructure and open chiplet economy -> /", "Claims 50x smaller, 10x less energy/bit, 10x lower upfront cost -> /", "Up to 50% reduction in chiplet die area -> /", "Wire abundant interfaces (1K / 0.25 mm\u00b2) -> /", "Ultra short reach (<500\u00b5m) -> /", "Die scale interconnect (sub-micron) -> /", "Protocol agnostic -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "CrossFire''s Bridgelet products provide the Chiplet to Chiplet interconnect currently provided by Interposers", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='crossfire-technologies-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Crown Technical Systems was founded in 1996 in Fontana, California, to address complex power distribution and control challenges for the utility industry. The company operates from three North American locations and has grown into a manufacturer of utility infrastructure that powers the digital world.

The company designs, fabricates, and integrates a range of power distribution products including medium‑voltage metal‑clad switchgear, protective relay control panels, and protective enclosures. It also builds power control assemblies, power distribution centers, and traction power substations. Fabrication services encompass steel construction, polyester outdoor powder coating, two‑part epoxy coatings (Carboline 890 and Maropoxy), dielectric floor coatings, and station‑service transformer and fuse integration. A team of engineers, fabricators, and skilled tradespeople works across the three facilities to deliver custom solutions, third‑party equipment integration, and turnkey systems.

Crown serves utilities, data centers, industrial facilities, transportation agencies, and renewable energy projects. Notable projects include control enclosures for the Vantage CA3 data center, equipment for Clark County Public Utilities, and systems for the San Diego Metropolitan Transit System.

