UPDATE companies SET description='The business traces its roots to 1958 when G.H. Lockhart founded G.H. Lockhart Sheet Metal to serve the HVAC industry across the Austin area. Lockhart’s crews handled major projects including the Federal Building, the downtown Austin Post Office, and Fort Hood. In 1993, longtime employee Ron Schwierking purchased the company and renamed it Custom Sheet Metal Inc., shifting its focus from union HVAC work to custom fabrication for a broader customer base. The company moved to its current Pflugerville facility in 2010, expanding its floor space and equipment capacity.

The shop specializes in sheet metal fabrication, offering shearing, forming, rolling, and welding across a range of metals: stainless steel, mild steel (cold‑rolled and hot‑rolled), aluminum, copper, brass, and galvanized sheet. The workforce carries over 100 years of combined experience in metalwork. Facility size, headcount, and annual volume are not disclosed.

While the company began in HVAC and industrial construction — supplying ductwork and components for large complexes — it now serves a wide variety of customers needing custom metal parts.

Schwierking’s stated goal was to maintain the integrity of the business through top‑notch craftsmanship and diligence. The company emphasizes fast turnaround times and high‑quality output as its primary differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sheet metal fabrication", "Shearing", "Forming", "Rolling", "Welding", "Custom fabrication", "Specialty fabrication"], "industries": ["HVAC", "Industrial construction", "Government", "Military", "Commercial construction"], "materials": ["Stainless Steel", "Mild Steel (Cold rolled)", "Mild Steel (Hot rolled)", "Aluminum", "Copper", "Brass", "Galvanized steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 100 years of combined workforce experience in metal fabrication", "Fast turnaround times on custom sheet metal parts", "In\u2011house shearing, forming, rolling, and welding capabilities", "Experience with government and military projects (Fort Hood, Federal Building)", "Expanded facility and equipment since 2010 relocation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1958 as G.H. Lockhart Sheet Metal -> /about", "Ron Schwierking purchased company in 1993 -> /about", "Moved to Pflugerville facility in 2010 -> /about", "Specializes in stainless steel, mild steel, aluminum, copper, brass, galvanized sheet -> /", "Processes: shear, form, roll, weld -> /", "Over 100 years combined workforce experience -> /", "Fastest turnaround times available -> /", "Past projects: Federal Building, Austin Post Office, Fort Hood -> /about", "Headquarters in Pflugerville, Texas -> db", "Company type: contract manufacturer/job shop -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Sheet Metal is a well equipped workshop in North Austin. ... CSMI can shear, form, roll, or weld any of the above mentioned materials.", "founded_year": "1958", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages":